@startuml
' Source block: uml251_08_interactions_sequence (uml-2.5.1-legend.puml intake)
!include ../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/interaction/sequence-diagram-style.iuml
' ============================================================================
' Section 08 — Interactions / Sequence Diagrams
'
' UML traceability:
'   UML 2.5.1 §17.2 Interactions
'   UML 2.5.1 §17.4 Lifelines
'   UML 2.5.1 §17.5 Messages
'   UML 2.5.1 §17.6 CombinedFragments
'   UML 2.5.1 §17.8 Sequence Diagrams
'
' PlantUML support: Native/Partial.
' Strict UML arrow style is requested to better align call arrowheads.
' ============================================================================

title UML 2.5.1 Notation Reference — Interactions and Sequence Diagrams
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam style strictuml
hide footbox

actor User
participant "Client" as Client
participant "Service" as Service
queue "Queue" as Queue

autonumber

[-> Client : found / incoming message\n(PlantUML boundary form)

Client -> Service : synchronousCall()
activate Service

Service -> Service : selfMessage()

Service ->> Queue : asynchronousSignal

alt accepted
  Service --> Client : reply / return
else rejected
  Service --> Client : error
end

opt auditing enabled
  Service -> Service : audit()
end

loop for each item
  Service -> Service : process(item)
end

par branch A
  Service -> Queue : publishA()
else branch B
  Service -> Queue : publishB()
end

critical update atomically
  Service -> Service : updateState()
end

break fatal condition
  Service --> Client : failure
end

ref over Client, Service : Reused Interaction / InteractionUse mapping

create Worker
Service -> Worker : create()
activate Worker
Worker -> Worker : selfCall()
Worker --> Service : done
destroy Worker

deactivate Service

Client ->x Service : lost message\n(PlantUML x marker)
Client ->] : outgoing message\n(outside shown scope)

note over Client,Service
  <b>UML message notation</b>
  • synchronous call: filled arrowhead
  • asynchronous message: open arrowhead
  • reply: dashed line
  • create: targets the created lifeline at its creation
  • delete: ends at a DestructionOccurrenceSpecification
  • found/lost UML messages use a black endpoint circle

  PlantUML's boundary arrows and final "x" syntax are
  renderer conventions; they are useful mappings but
  are not identical to every UML found/lost endpoint glyph.
end note

legend
  |= UML interaction concept |= PlantUML mapping |
  | Lifeline / Actor lifeline | participant / actor — Native |
  | ExecutionSpecification | activate/deactivate — Native |
  | Synchronous call | -> with strictuml — Native |
  | Asynchronous message | ->> — Native |
  | Reply | --> / return — Native |
  | Create | create + first received message — Native |
  | Destruction | destroy / !! — Native |
  | Self message | participant -> itself — Native |
  | Found / lost message | boundary arrow / x marker — Partial |
  | CombinedFragment alt/opt/loop/par/break/critical | matching grouping keywords — Native |
  | InteractionUse | ref over — Partial/native visual mapping |
endlegend
@enduml
